This port
---------
Copyright (C) 2026  Marc Balcells

This port is a translation of the Galaxia 0.7.2 C++ source into Rust, with modifications,
including (non-exhaustively): a different pseudo-random number generator (counter-based
Philox4x32-10 instead of drand48), a multi-threaded batch mode that loads the model data once,
deterministic per-field random streams, an output provenance record, stricter input validation
and error handling, and optional (experimental) CUDA and OpenCL backends. Output is therefore
statistically, not bit-wise, equivalent to the original; see VALIDATION.md.

The port is distributed under the same licence as the original: GNU Affero General Public
License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version (SPDX: AGPL-3.0-or-later). The full
licence text is in the file LICENSE. Because the AGPL applies, if you run a modified version
as a network service you must offer its source to its users.

Data
----
The Galaxia data files (`GalaxiaData`: BHTrees, Padova isochrones, extinction maps, ...) are NOT
part of this repository and are not redistributed. Obtain them from the original Galaxia
distribution (http://galaxia.sourceforge.net) and observe their terms.

Included third-party material
-----------------------------
`src/backend/cuda/kernels/spawn.ptx` is NVIDIA PTX assembly generated by `nvcc` from
`src/backend/cuda/kernels/spawn.cu` in this repository (experimental CUDA backend only).
